[ledge] Functional lower spring-hook bearing after the lead-exit opening: the retained aft hook has 0.60 mm engagement plus 0.25 mm running allowance and a 3 mm spring wall. Its fore end stays open for the meter lead. Tree(auto)/Default approaches through the cap’s open mouth before assembly.
alternatives: Sloping the bearing provides a withdrawal ramp; filling the fore opening blocks the lead path. A 3 mm reach requires another 2.15 mm of spring travel and larger matching pockets.
